# Neptuno: active-seat access to input event nodes.
#
# Niri has no org.freedesktop.portal.GlobalShortcuts backend, so evdev consumers
# (DMS's evdev manager for modifier/Caps Lock state, HEX dictation) must read
# /dev/input/event* directly. Upstream's answer is "join the input group", which
# does not stick on this image: `input` is defined only in /usr/lib/group and
# resolved through nss-altfiles, so `usermod -aG input` exits 0 without writing
# a membership into /etc/group (the only file shadow-utils edits).
#
# TAG+="uaccess" makes systemd's uaccess builtin attach an ACL for the user of
# the active seat session: effective at login with no re-login, revoked when the
# session ends, and never inherited by remote SSH sessions.
#
# Security: read access to event* is keyboard-read capability, i.e. keylogger
# equivalent for the logged-in user. Accepted deliberately for this image;
# Fedora tags only joysticks with uaccess, not keyboards.
#
# The filename must sort before 73-seat-late.rules, which is what runs the
# uaccess builtin; a 73+ number sets the tag too late for the ACL to be applied.
# ACTION!="remove" keeps the tag applied on "change" events too (systemd >= 258).
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", TAG+="uaccess"
